  - given-names: Harrison
    family-names: Bai
    email: harrison.bai@cuanschutz.edu
    affiliation: Department of Radiology, University of Colorado Anschutz School of Medicine
repository-code: https://github.com/Yangxinyee/ehr2trace
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.6.0
abstract: >-
  EHR2Trace converts local hospital EHR extracts (delimited text and spreadsheets)
  into OMOP CDM 5.4 and MEDS. The two targets are derived independently from a
  single canonical layer rather than one from the other, every published row
  carries a link back to the source rows it came from, and forty checks encode
  the properties a conversion must satisfy before it can be used as training
  data -- including the leakage failures that are invisible to schema validation.
  Where the data does not answer a question, the converter blocks and says so
  instead of substituting a default.
keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - MEDS
  - electronic health records
  - data provenance
  - ETL validation
  - clinical machine learning
